## Problem

Users could bypass RBAC permission checks after viewing/editing entities. A user with Viewer+Seller roles could create products despite lacking `Products.Create` permission.

## Root Cause

`EnableForm(false)` unconditionally re-enabled action buttons (New, Edit, Delete) without re-checking permissions:

```csharp
// Before: Permission bypass
private void EnableForm(bool enabled)
{
    grpDetails.Enabled = enabled;
    grpList.Enabled = !enabled;
    btnNew.Enabled = !enabled;     // ❌ Ignores ConfigurePermissions()
    btnEdit.Enabled = !enabled;    // ❌ Ignores ConfigurePermissions()
    btnDelete.Enabled = !enabled;  // ❌ Ignores ConfigurePermissions()
}
```

## Solution

Re-apply permission checks when transitioning back to list view:

```csharp
// After: Permissions enforced
private void EnableForm(bool enabled)
{
    grpDetails.Enabled = enabled;
    grpList.Enabled = !enabled;

    if (!enabled)
    {
        ConfigurePermissions();  // ✅ Re-checks user permissions
    }
}
```

## Affected Forms

- **ProductsForm** - Products.Create/Edit/Delete
- **UsersForm** - Users.Create/Edit/Delete/ChangePassword/AssignRoles
- **WarehousesForm** - Warehouses.Create/Edit/Delete
- **RolesForm** - Roles.Create/Edit/Delete/ManagePermissions
- **SalesForm** - Sales.Create
- **StockMovementForm** - Stock.Receive/Issue/Transfer/Adjust

## Impact

Permission checks now consistently enforced across all form state transitions. Users cannot escalate privileges through UI interaction patterns.

